# The kodiak reference headers are raw binary and must stay BYTE-EXACT.
#
# The repo's own .gitattributes marks `.github/boot-template/*.bin` as binary, but that glob
# does not cross the '/' into this subdirectory, so without this file git on a Windows box
# (core.autocrlf=true) may treat them as text and rewrite CRLF sequences. They are the 4 KB
# header dumps that verify_boot_img.py compares against, so any rewrite silently changes the
# thing the build is verified against.
.github/boot-template/kodiak/*.bin binary
